// NICHE TEMPLATES — written, vetted reference Q&A for specific niches.
// One entry per finished template, entered ONCE by hand — never generated
// or edited at runtime.
//
// "aliases" — short, common alternate phrasings someone might actually
// type or pick for this niche on the canvas. Checked for an exact match
// BEFORE the AI fuzzy match in matchNicheToTemplate below — skips the
// Mistral call entirely for the common case, and removes any
// hallucination risk for it.
//
// "questions" MUST be 44 entries long, in the EXACT same order as
// IDEATION_SCAFFOLD (same 9 blocks, same 5-per-block order). Each entry is
// tagged with its own "block" — not just inferred from array position —
// so getTemplateReference() below can assert the tag actually matches what
// IDEATION_SCAFFOLD expects at that index. Manual transcription of 45
// question/option blocks is exactly the kind of process that can lose or
// reorder an entry without anyone noticing; this turns that into a loud
// console.error instead of silently feeding the WRONG block's reference
// into a question.
//
// "description" is used by matchNicheToTemplate below so the AI fuzzy-
// match fallback works off real semantic meaning, not just a bare string.
//
// This is grounding data for the live question generator (see
// generateIdeationQuestion below), not a replacement for it — the model
// still writes every question fresh, every time. A matched template just
// gives it one concrete, already-vetted example of how that exact slot
// was handled for a similar niche, instead of only the abstract intent.
// ============================================================
